{
  "fixture": "good/release_fencing.json",
  "contract": "mcp/DISCOVERY_V1.md",
  "kind": "fence",
  "exercises": "The record of good/unavailable_pause_reason.json, released by reconciliation on instance A while instance B holds the job's live lease. The release is a normal record save: it leaves B's lease, fence and attempt as they are, so B's next commit, with that very fence, is refused DISCOVERY_UNAVAILABLE and writes nothing. That refusal is thrown inside B's checkpoint sink: the scheduler keeps it and rethrows it as it was, so B's pause carries its cause and log (not a worker reply, so C1 does not check it) and sets the fence null, keeping the attempt. A commit from an older attempt is refused STALE_ATTEMPT first, as today. A queued job becomes paused with a null fence and keeps its attempt counter, its queued_at, its queue_order and its cancel_requested; a paused job keeps its attempt. Nothing resets a fence on a job some instance holds.",
  "expect": {
    "accepted": true
  },
